{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again","id":1540831,"title":"Vampire: Bloodlines 2 Videogame Delayed (Again)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-21T06:25:13-07:00","id":1540831,"title":"Vampire: Bloodlines 2 Videogame Delayed (Again)","content":"In not so surprising news for anyone who has been following Bloodlines 2, Paradox/Chinese Room announced that the game Bloodlines 2's release is gonna be delayed again. The <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/whats-next-for-bloodlines-2\" target=\"_blank\">blog-post/video</a> shares more details:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good evening,<br /> <br /> Today, The Chinese Room\u2019s Alex Skidmore, Creative Director for Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2, and Mattias Lilja, Deputy CEO for Paradox Interactive, share an update on Bloodlines 2.<br /> <br /> To quickly recap, Mattias and Alex share:<ul><li>Bloodlines 2\u2019s release window has been updated to the first half of 2025.</li> <li>Paradox and The Chinese Room\u2019s commitment to delivering a high-quality action RPG for Vampire fans, new and old.</li> <li>Some of the things they're excited about working on with the additional time.</li> </ul>What will the additional time be used for?<br /> <br /> It will be used to create a quality assurance buffer, giving more time between testing and launch, ensuring we release the game when it\u2019s ready. The extra time gives us an opportunity to adjust certain areas, such as Fabien, and incorporate other community feedback.<br /> <br /> We will also use the time to expand the game\u2019s story, and now Bloodlines 2 will have more than twice as many endings as its predecessor.\u200b </div> </div> </div>&quot;First half of the year&quot; probably means that the actual release-date will be something like May or July. It's the right decision, though, as nothing in the previews indicated that the game was ready for release.<br /> <br /> As a bit of an aside, I wanna mention this post I made a while ago again about the state of Paradox in 2024:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538120#post1538120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Paradox as a company is a bad one. It's only thanks to a few of their games which are these juggernauts on the market that they stay profitable. Aside from those, namely Hearts of Iron IV, Crusader Kings 3 and Stellaris, Paradox as a company would be in a world of trouble. If there's anything that has been a constant in the last few years, it's them fucking up as a publisher.<br /> <br /> Let's go over some of the highlights over the last few years:<ul><li>Lamplighter's Leauge: Paradox had high hopes for the game and Harebrained Games are a good developer (they made those isometric Shadowrun games, for example). But months before the launch, thanks to a lack of support from Paradox 80% of the staff at the studio were let go. Then the game got released to middling reviews (mostly because of the bugs and lack of content) and then Paradox had to announce that it considered <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/paradox-says-the-lamplighters-league-sales-were-a-big-disappointment-confirms-recent-layoffs-at-developer-harebrained-schemes/\" target=\"_blank\">the game a failure</a>. And it doesn't seem like there's any more content planned for it.</li> <li>City Skylines 2: That game launched in a disastrous state. Just google it. A complete failure. The developers are still busy trying to crawl out of that hole and win back the goodwill of the players...</li> <li>Star Trek Infinite: One of the more popular mods for their Sci-Fi-grand strategy game Stellaris revolves around Star Trek. And so Paradox thought: Hey, let's have someone develop an official version. And that's Star Trek Infinite except... the fan-mods are simply better. The game launches, disappoints (middling reviews, lack of interest, sales...) and six months after launch it's announced that <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/paradoxs-grand-strategy-star-trek-infinite-will-receive-no-further-updates\" target=\"_blank\">Paradox will stop any support for the game</a>. In other words, Paradox isn't paying the devs to patch the game or make DLC for it.</li> <li>Life By You: It was pitched as a new Sims-type life-building game. They even created a studio for it called Tectone. Well, a month ago or so, Paradox announced it had decided to <a href=\"https://news.cision.com/paradox-interactive-ab/r/paradox-interactive-cancels-the-release-of-life-by-you-which-impacts-the-second-quarter-with-msek-20,c4002478\" target=\"_blank\">cancel the game</a>. This game had been in development since 2019. Five years of development, a whole studio of developers and 19 million dollars in investment... all flushed down the toilet. Ah, yeah, they closed the studio Tectone as well on top of that.</li> </ul><br /> Bloodlines 2 turning out to be a failure wouldn't be that surprising.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> The reason I wanna highlight this again is that in addition to Bloodlines 2's delay mentioned at the start, you can add yet another game to this list which is being published by Paradox: Prison Architect 2:<ul><li>Despite previous delays, the game's release-date is now changed to &quot;unknown&quot;. It seems like there's still a lot of work ahead for the developers. (source: <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/strategy/paradox-indefinitely-delays-prison-architect-2-just-like-it-did-with-life-by-you-before-it-was-scrapped/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Paradox indefinitely delays Prison Architect 2, just like it did with Life By You before it was scrapped&quot;</a>)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T09:34:16-07:00","id":1540845,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this is good news to me. The last gameplay footage I saw a while ago didn\u2019t convince me at all, so good on them if they take the time they need rather than rush it.<br /> <br /> At this point, however, I have zero expectation. While it certainly would be nice to have another VTM game, the game could be cancelled again and I wouldn\u2019t even be disappointed. This way if it ends up cancelled or terrible I\u2019ll forget about it, and if it ends up being a good game I\u2019ll be pleasantly surprised.<br /> <br /> Guess, we\u2019ll see.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T15:55:04-07:00","id":1540861,"title":"","content":"Considering the quality of writing to match Bloodlines 1 and the fact that VtM really is a Gen X thing which doesn't easily translate to millennials, zoomers, and now gen alphas... I would say this is losing proposition regardless of what is done.<br /> <br /> Honestly, a more profitable video game would be just to make a tongue in cheek dating sim like &quot;Hooked On You&quot; from the Dead by Daylight franchise. Though given some of the writing in the currently out visual novel game for VtM, that might be a stretch as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T17:33:52-07:00","id":1540864,"title":"","content":"Guys, don't worry. Bloodlines 2 will be released... soon after Blade with Maharshala Ali premiers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T18:13:52-07:00","id":1540868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1540845#post1540845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, this is good news to me. The last gameplay footage I saw a while ago didn\u2019t convince me at all, so good on them if they take the time they need rather than rush it.<br /> <br /> At this point, however, I have zero expectation. While it certainly would be nice to have another VTM game, the game could be cancelled again and I wouldn\u2019t even be disappointed. This way if it ends up cancelled or terrible I\u2019ll forget about it, and if it ends up being a good game I\u2019ll be pleasantly surprised.<br /> <br /> Guess, we\u2019ll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. At this point all expectation is dead, so whatever. It isn't as if they had to launch soon to capitalize on hype, as that would have been years ago.<br /> <br /> Worst case scenario they would cancel it to save some money, but by this point and given that this is a pet project on top of it all, trying to make a late but good game may be a less stupid move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T19:46:39-07:00","id":1540870,"title":"","content":"Not a surprise. By all means they should take as long as they want to finish it. The hype is completely dead, so there's no need to rush the release. They just need to make as good of a game as they possibly can. I doubt we'll get anything particularly stellar no matter how long they take, so as long as it's not bad that will be good enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T08:51:51-07:00","id":1540895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1540868#post1540868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. At this point all expectation is dead, so whatever. It isn't as if they had to launch soon to capitalize on hype, as that would have been years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if the game end up being just decent i might end up enjoying it more now that any hope i ever had of it being good has been killed and buried twice.<br /> I\u2019ve come to realize that hype generally makes my overall experience worse for games or movies as they set the bar high and it almost never live to the expectations.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t watched any gameplay footage in a long while, i just hope they don\u2019t go full First Person mode, i enjoy the third person view more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T10:57:49-07:00","id":1540901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1540864#post1540864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, don't worry. Bloodlines 2 will be released... soon after Blade with Maharshala Ali premiers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, it could be when Maharshala Ali will be old enough to collect a pension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T04:05:26-07:00","id":1540935,"title":"","content":"I remember buying my desktop computer, at this point it must be at least five years ago, selecting it specifically hoping to play this game.<br /> <br /> I do hope it gets released, but like others have said, I feel just completely confused about the direction this game is taking, how these last few trailers make the game not feel like Vampire the Masquerade at all. The trailers mostly contained first person combat using hands and fists and weird difficult to interpret hand movement / blood magic. It felts like they were trying to sell the game on being a Cyberpunk-like heavy combat game, which just doesnt appeal to me at all.<br /> <br /> Apart from that we\u2019ve only seen one or two scene of dialogue between the main character and one Nosferatu, seemingly with less control over what is being said than in the original game.<br /> <br /> I wish they stayed more true to the concept and genre of the original.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7279-ichneumon","user":"Ichneumon","date":". 08-23-2024, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7279-ichneumon","name":"Ichneumon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7279_6.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T22:12:30-07:00","id":1541379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1540861#post1540861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtM really is a Gen X thing</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hate it when people say this. VTM's themes have only gotten more relevant since the 90's(Railing against Misinformation, government secrecy and overreach, soulless life-draining corporations, and the destruction of freedoms for the sake of benefiting the &quot;elites&quot; will probably always be relevant).<br /> <br /> The setting can easily work closer to modern times. Current issue have more than proven that mass surveillance and the proliferation of smartphones isn't the killing blow to the masquerade we thought it would be in the early 2000s. Cover-up are actually easier than ever now that no one actually knows their neighbors anymore, all news sources are own by a small list of people, and nearly all info on the internet is filtered by algorythms that we already Know are programmed to hide things from us. The masquerade would only be More believable now.<br /> <br /> The only thing holding the setting back is the writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T04:29:48-07:00","id":1541389,"title":"","content":"It was pretty obvious it was not coming out on time. A game of that scope with that little to show could not have been wrapped up by the end of the year. Hopefully they manage to use their time and make something better out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T11:13:14-07:00","id":1541401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541379#post1541379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hate it when people say this. VTM's themes have only gotten more relevant since the 90's(Railing against Misinformation, government secrecy and overreach, soulless life-draining corporations, and the destruction of freedoms for the sake of benefiting the &quot;elites&quot; will probably always be relevant).<br /> <br /> The setting can easily work closer to modern times. Current issue have more than proven that mass surveillance and the proliferation of smartphones isn't the killing blow to the masquerade we thought it would be in the early 2000s. Cover-up are actually easier than ever now that no one actually knows their neighbors anymore, all news sources are own by a small list of people, and nearly all info on the internet is filtered by algorythms that we already Know are programmed to hide things from us. The masquerade would only be More believable now.<br /> <br /> The only thing holding the setting back is the writers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are missing my point when I say &quot;VtM is a Gen X thing&quot;. I agree completely that many of the themes are still relevant today if not more so.<br /> <br /> But what I am talking about is the people who inhabit those times and what they are rebelling against.<br /> <br /> VtM came out in the same era when the Cranberries released Zombie (a cultural touchstone for the Irish), REM released Losing My Religion which back then was rather taboo concept, the early 90s were still having aftershocks of the satanic panic and the religious groups burning D&amp;D books. We had the Bosnian genocide going on and Tiananmen square was still fresh in everyone's minds.<br /> <br /> The current crop of generations commemorate their struggles on social media with breaking down in tears at the concept of an 8-hour shift at starbucks, raging over the fact that other people don't believe in their pronouns, or being so socially stunted that the idea of talking to someone in person gives them anxiety on a generational level.<br /> <br /> As you can see this is night and day differences in cultural priorities between the different eras and generations. Now I don't consider this a bad thing, I look back at the 1960s &amp; the hippies and just don't get it, much to the annoyance of those who were there at the time.<br /> <br /> I agree the writers are a big part of the problem, but I feel it is a question of focus rather than inherent skill. VtM was created in a very specific cultural flavor which has now passed into history. The writers have a few choices to make with each new edition, do they cater to the original flavor and just work on improving the mechanics, or do they try to mutate the source material to fit whatever the current era is?<br /> <br /> The answer is to refine the mechanics, but not treat any era as the default. Just release splat books for eras that explains how each clan adjusts and how play styles change with advancing technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T12:49:50-07:00","id":1541402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541401#post1541401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current crop of generations commemorate their struggles on social media with breaking down in tears at the concept of an 8-hour shift at starbucks, raging over the fact that other people don't believe in their pronouns, or being so socially stunted that the idea of talking to someone in person gives them anxiety on a generational level.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you genuinely think this is the face of the current generation, then I think you need to turn off your computer and go outside. Social media is an amplifier for all the worst parts of any group, simply because that very reliably generates clicks and social media only cares about clicks.<br /> <br /> Need I remind you there's active wars in europe and isreal, with another one brewing between america and china? That the last 5 years was punctuated by riots, protests, and political unrest that's going to be their own sections in people's history books? The largest natural disasters in Centuries(I'm still bewildered the people have forgotten the real life <i>Fire Tornado</i>)?<br /> <br /> &quot;These Generations&quot; have all the issues with the powerful, the will to fight back, and all the other hallmarks that build Punk in the first place, but are absolutely being painted as strawmen by a monopolistic legacy media owned by the generation of people famous for doing that to every generation after them. This should feel familiar considering this is Exactly what was happening in the 90's when legacy media was leaning mostly right rather than mostly left. It's the same song and dance with the actors shuffled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T13:23:09-07:00","id":1541404,"title":"","content":"if VTM is a Gen X thing, why is one of the most popular characters in Baldurs gate 3 Astarion? One of the better Toreador or Thin blood depictions i have seen? Vampires are still very much active in our Zeitgeist. Maybe they are more metrosexual and or soft, but w/e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T14:14:08-07:00","id":1541405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541402#post1541402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you genuinely think this is the face of the current generation, then I think you need to turn off your computer and go outside. Social media is an amplifier for all the worst parts of any group, simply because that very reliably generates clicks and social media only cares about clicks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never had social media, I just get bombarded by its fall out every time people open their mouths. If you truly think that people take pride in their work, truly believe in giving a fair days work for a fair days pay, or have good manners and know how to act in a civil manner, then you really need to look into history more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541402#post1541402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Need I remind you there's active wars in europe and isreal, with another one brewing between america and china? That the last 5 years was punctuated by riots, protests, and political unrest that's going to be their own sections in people's history books? The largest natural disasters in Centuries(I'm still bewildered the people have forgotten the real life <i>Fire Tornado</i>)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Active conflicts, after WWI and WWII, we more or less redefined the scale when it comes to wars. Both Korea and Viet Nam were only classified as &quot;police actions&quot; rather than wars for the longest time due to their limited scale. But despite us having more access to information and knowledge of what is going on, we are seeing absolutely pathetic enlistment numbers, because no one feels they should go and do something about those problems, or at least they seem to think that raging on the internet from the safety of their home is more than enough.<br /> <br /> What does natural disasters have to do with anything? Are we measuring the cultural impact of a fire tornado verses the Loma Prieta earthquake as to which traumatized more people or something?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it is a matter of perspective, for the younger crowd yeah, the last five years have been kind of crazy. But if you are older, the last five years have been just the latest round of issues, in other words, Tuesday.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541402#post1541402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;These Generations&quot; have all the issues with the powerful, the will to fight back, and all the other hallmarks that build Punk in the first place, but are absolutely being painted as strawmen by a monopolistic legacy media owned by the generation of people famous for doing that to every generation after them. This should feel familiar considering this is Exactly what was happening in the 90's when legacy media was leaning mostly right rather than mostly left. It's the same song and dance with the actors shuffled.</div> </div> </div> </div>You couldn't be more wrong. The 80s &amp; 90s media is what everything has been ripping off for the past 20+ years because it was original. What the 80s and early 90s people were fighting against was not corporate overlords, that was more late 90s to early 2000s.<br /> <br /> A better way to look at it is that offspring inherently tend to rebel against their parent's values and teachings if for no other reason than to test if they are still valid as a survival strategy. Eventually the offspring settle down and follow what works, the problem is that the parents often pass along their biases on top of their values. In the context of Gen X, their parents who were Baby Boomers aka Hippies, taught the children to reject the cultural concepts of the silent generation and earlier ones.<br /> <br /> So, a Gen Xer rejects the 60's revolution as being a bunch of spiritual BS that didn't fix anything, but they were indoctrinated to inherently reject the power structures of the grandparent's era by the parents. The result is that Gen Xers were at odds with and rebelling against everything. This promoted a very &quot;stand on your own or die trying&quot; type of mentality. By comparison the modern generations are far more medicated, far more neurotic, require far more therapy, and have remarkably less autonomy despite having more options than any other generation in history.<br /> <br /> Now apply that to VtM, the PC is at odds with mortal society because they are undead, they are at odds with the older vampires because they can't compete with their influence or power, they are at odds with their fellow young vampires because everyone is biting and clawing to survive. The only one you can depend on is yourself, and the people around you may or may not double cross you to get ahead. Sounds a lot more like a Gen X point of view than a Millennial, Gen Z, or even Gen Alpha thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T14:15:44-07:00","id":1541406,"title":"","content":"There's always been a sexual motif in vampire lore and after a certain age many mortal things fall to the way side. I remember Mick Farren trilogy of vampire novels and how the oldest was starting to move beyond physical contact when he felt a stirring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T14:45:01-07:00","id":1541408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541404#post1541404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if VTM is a Gen X thing, why is one of the most popular characters in Baldurs gate 3 Astarion? One of the better Toreador or Thin blood depictions i have seen? Vampires are still very much active in our Zeitgeist. Maybe they are more metrosexual and or soft, but w/e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't played BG3 so I don't know how the story interacts with Astarions character. As far as my perception of Astarion from trailers or lets plays, he feels more like style over substance and come backs rather than competence. Take away his vampiric status, and he looks and behaves like an elf being played by a theater kid in high school.<br /> <br /> Perhaps due to my own background with art and antiques, I have never fully accepted the concept of the Toreador are artists and thus they must fit the psychological profile of a hedonistic metrosexual social butterfly. For every passionate artist who is seeking their next muse, there is an artist who functions by focusing entirely on the refinement of their skills. Less &quot;Piss Christ&quot; and more &quot;old dutch masters&quot; or greek and roman sculptors. Though you could make an argument that impressionism more or less killed the &quot;personal skill&quot; refinement aspect of art in the western world.<br /> <br /> If we were to use the same sort of lens on the Brujah as you are suggesting for the Toreador or thin-bloods, then all Brujah would simply be socialists. Rather than being idealists who want change. A Brujah can just as easily be full on communist as they can be fire and brimstone type arguing for the return to traditional values when residing in a culture that has gotten very hedonistic.<br /> <br /> Great, now I am imagining Ben Shapiro or Candice Owens with fangs, and for some reason that is less scary and more amusing in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T14:52:34-07:00","id":1541409,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Off-topic, deleting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-02-2024, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T15:22:28-07:00","id":1541411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541405#post1541405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never had social media, I just get bombarded by its fall out every time people open their mouths. If you truly think that people take pride in their work, truly believe in giving a fair days work for a fair days pay, or have good manners and know how to act in a civil manner, then you really need to look into history more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh look an old man yelling at clouds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Active conflicts, after WWI and WWII, we more or less redefined the scale when it comes to wars. Both Korea and Viet Nam were only classified as &quot;police actions&quot; rather than wars for the longest time due to their limited scale. But despite us having more access to information and knowledge of what is going on, we are seeing absolutely pathetic enlistment numbers, because no one feels they should go and do something about those problems, or at least they seem to think that raging on the internet from the safety of their home is more than enough. </div> </div> </div>A distinction only cropping up to denote how it's still a limited exchange and the nukes aren't flying. For the dead, it doesn't exactly matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does natural disasters have to do with anything? Are we measuring the cultural impact of a fire tornado verses the Loma Prieta earthquake as to which traumatized more people or something? </div> </div> </div>Expect more of them, in more extreme form, as humans continue burning off the storehouse of Carboniferous-era carbon reserves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I think it is a matter of perspective, for the younger crowd yeah, the last five years have been kind of crazy. But if you are older, the last five years have been just the latest round of issues, in other words, Tuesday. </div> </div> </div>Well, when it comes to disasters, it's often the case that no one is old enough to recall when things were really crazy. But nowadays, century events are becoming decade events, and decade events are nearly every year.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You couldn't be more wrong. The 80s &amp; 90s media is what everything has been ripping off for the past 20+ years because it was original. </div> </div> </div>Really? Ripping off Anne Rice and Brian Lumley makes you original?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What the 80s and early 90s people were fighting against was not corporate overlords, that was more late 90s to early 2000s. </div> </div> </div>In other words far too late.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A better way to look at it is that offspring inherently tend to rebel against their parent's values and teachings if for no other reason than to test if they are still valid as a survival strategy. Eventually the offspring settle down and follow what works, the problem is that the parents often pass along their biases on top of their values. In the context of Gen X, their parents who were Baby Boomers aka Hippies, taught the children to reject the cultural concepts of the silent generation and earlier ones. </div> </div> </div>Except for the ones that think that everything against the mores of the 50s was communism and thus evil. Or the ones who were mostly apathetic to that. If it was that widespread, there wouldn't have been a massive civil rights movement.<br /> <br /> (Also, this is getting very US-specific)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, a Gen Xer rejects the 60's revolution as being a bunch of spiritual BS that didn't fix anything, but they were indoctrinated to inherently reject the power structures of the grandparent's era by the parents. </div> </div> </div>No, their parents and prior generations thought that they were lazy and worthless and thought little of them. That's the entire conceit behind calling them &quot;Generation X&quot;. That was the butt of the joke in The Critic's &quot;Star Trek: Generation X&quot; quick clip joke.<br /> <br /> Picard: &quot;Alright, which one of you wrote 'Beavis and Butthead rule!' on the back of my skullcap?&quot;<br /> <br /> Whatever the characters that Keanu Reeves and Christian Slater are playing: &quot;Uh, not us.&quot; [Both laugh exactly like Beavis and Butthead]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The result is that Gen Xers were at odds with and rebelling against everything. This promoted a very &quot;stand on your own or die trying&quot; type of mentality. By comparison the modern generations are far more medicated, far more neurotic, require far more therapy, and have remarkably less autonomy despite having more options than any other generation in history. </div> </div> </div>Back in the day, no one got therapy and they were fucked up for that lack. Prior generations didn't &quot;do fine&quot; without it; they had a shitload of terrible coping mechanisms that they didn't discuss and took shit to a grave while ensuring that everyone else around them was dragged down with them. What's more, all of the conditions that we recognize now still existed, and the only change has been how they've been considered and discussed. They aren't more prevalent in modern times; we've just gotten better at diagnostics and don't disregard them as being &quot;fucking weird&quot; or whatever less passable language would have been used at the time.<br /> <br /> As for autonomy, the US has always chained that to money, and last I checked, anyone born after Gen X is unlikely to be ever in a position where they can own a house because the ladder got kicked out by the people who climbed up it. The 80s were full of policies that failed here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now apply that to VtM, the PC is at odds with mortal society because they are undead, they are at odds with the older vampires because they can't compete with their influence or power, they are at odds with their fellow young vampires because everyone is biting and clawing to survive. The only one you can depend on is yourself, and the people around you may or may not double cross you to get ahead. Sounds a lot more like a Gen X point of view than a Millennial, Gen Z, or even Gen Alpha thing. </div> </div> </div>This was around back when Gen X would have been fresh 20-somethings, long before there were any other generational struggles of that kind in sight (because in 1991, people who were born in 1992 to 2022 weren't even remotely around to being born yet and Vampire didn't care about kids). Also, the &quot;you can only rely on yourself&quot; is probably at least partially because the US education system is trying really, really hard to get you to be a factory worker who doesn't bother the supervisor with shit.<br /> <br /> And, in the end, just a year later, the other games in the WoD started dropping, and none of them had this same take. In fact, from Werewolf to Changeling, it gave the middle finger to various parts or even the whole of Vampire's shallow, cynical take (even as dark as Wraith is, it questioned if you could actually rely on yourself when you have the self-destructive Shadow deceiving you at every turn to get you to succumb to Oblivion). All this &quot;the Millenial youngin's ruined Vampire!&quot; shit is insular and Vampire-centered brain rot, plain and simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T22:53:50-07:00","id":1541433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541411#post1541411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Ripping off Anne Rice and Brian Lumley makes you original?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, because they in turn weren't ripping off Bram Stoker, Sheridan Le Fanu, and Lovecraft. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541411#post1541411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, their parents and prior generations thought that they were lazy and worthless and thought little of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small spoiler, every generation finds the next one lacking. When the new generation has survived long enough, been through enough, and successfully raised yet another generation, then the older one might give some begrudging respect, assuming the older generation got to survive long enough to see it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541411#post1541411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in the day, no one got therapy and they were fucked up for that lack. Prior generations didn't &quot;do fine&quot; without it; they had a shitload of terrible coping mechanisms that they didn't discuss and took shit to a grave while ensuring that everyone else around them was dragged down with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't make me laugh, the fields of psychology and psychotherapy have never been able to stand up to rigorous scrutiny. Just take a look at the Rosenham experiments, particularly the second one which proved the professionals couldn't actually figure out who actually had a problem. The modern obsession with &quot;Therapy&quot; is more of a validation tactic than anything else. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541411#post1541411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's more, all of the conditions that we recognize now still existed, and the only change has been how they've been considered and discussed. They aren't more prevalent in modern times; we've just gotten better at diagnostics and don't disregard them as being &quot;fucking weird&quot; or whatever less passable language would have been used at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>While things like functional MRIs, a better understanding of gut biome to brain interaction, and the interactions of things like genes and epigenetics has advanced out understanding of how our minds work, we have yet to create a truly functional methodology for dealing with these issues. The ability to self-diagnose and or self-identify functionally proves that we have no viable criteria for such things, which in turn means the &quot;therapists&quot; are more or less fumbling around in the dark and doing whatever keeps someone in therapy rather than moving on in life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541411#post1541411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for autonomy, the US has always chained that to money, and last I checked, anyone born after Gen X is unlikely to be ever in a position where they can own a house because the ladder got kicked out by the people who climbed up it. The 80s were full of policies that failed here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well when you destroy the concepts of the nuclear family, the concept of traditional community, and focus on feelings rather than tangible results, I have a hard time seeing the outcome as being beneficial.<br /> <br /> Money has been the benchmark for autonomy for most of human civilization because it allowed you to trade without having a specific trade good. Thus, you could hire experts to do things for you rather than learning and doing them yourself. Governmental Policy is supposed to be a fall-back measure rather than an individual's blank check to succeed in life.<br /> <br /> Think of it like this, do you depend on the government to regulate all food prices, regulate all pay rates, and ensure the distribution networks, or do you grow your own food? It is the individual who looks at the situation, comes up with a plan that doesn't depend on any one thing to fill their needs, and modulates their choices as needed. I am not saying everyone needs to be a farmer, but I am calling out the people who think they can have it all without understanding how things work or could go wrong, and thus fail to plan accordingly. <br /> <br /> Prior to WWII most people lived in rural areas rather than cities, the concept of turning 18 and leaving was more plot hook than normal behavior. Multiple generations lived under the same roof, they all pitched in to try to survive. The family farm or business was handed down generation to generation because almost no one could afford to go somewhere else and start from scratch. Doing so was such a momentous thing that we practically mythologized the action in our cultural narrative.<br /> <br /> When you are saying that no one can afford a house these days and that is proof that things are unfair, what you are really railing against is the fact that the notion of everyone being able to afford their own home was a cultural hiccup that only lasted about 50 years and has come to a close.<br /> <br /> On a related note, if all of the Silent Generation, Baby Boomers, and Gen Xers have bought houses, how do the Millennials and Gen Z fail to own homes? They should be inheriting them if nothing else. The answer is that the newer generations sold those houses because they wanted to follow their dreams, move somewhere else, rather than realizing what they truly had. There is an argument that things get complicated with splitting inheritance between multiple offspring, but the birth rate has tanked so badly that there generally aren't siblings in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T09:03:26-07:00","id":1541454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541408#post1541408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't played BG3 so I don't know how the story interacts with Astarions character. As far as my perception of Astarion from trailers or lets plays, he feels more like style over substance and come backs rather than competence. Take away his vampiric status, and he looks and behaves like an elf being played by a theater kid in high school.<br /> <br /> Perhaps due to my own background with art and antiques, I have never fully accepted the concept of the Toreador are artists and thus they must fit the psychological profile of a hedonistic metrosexual social butterfly. For every passionate artist who is seeking their next muse, there is an artist who functions by focusing entirely on the refinement of their skills. Less &quot;Piss Christ&quot; and more &quot;old dutch masters&quot; or greek and roman sculptors. Though you could make an argument that impressionism more or less killed the &quot;personal skill&quot; refinement aspect of art in the western world.<br /> <br /> If we were to use the same sort of lens on the Brujah as you are suggesting for the Toreador or thin-bloods, then all Brujah would simply be socialists. Rather than being idealists who want change. A Brujah can just as easily be full on communist as they can be fire and brimstone type arguing for the return to traditional values when residing in a culture that has gotten very hedonistic.<br /> <br /> Great, now I am imagining Ben Shapiro or Candice Owens with fangs, and for some reason that is less scary and more amusing in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>BG3 Spoilers regarding Astarion<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Astarion is a high elf vampire spawn, which means he was turned into a vampire and forced into servitude for centuries by a cruel vampire lord named Cazador Szarr (Blood bond wink wink, nodge nodge). Despite this trauma, Astarion's charm, wit and flirtatious personality make him a great character. What actually makes him interesting is that throughtout the game hestruggles with the trauma of his past and the desire for freedom, as well as the moral implications of embracing or rejecting his darker nature, his ascension. If Astarion chooses to pursue ascension, he fully embraces a brutal vampiric nature, gaining immense power and the ability to control other vampire spawn. This also leads to a significant moral shift, as Astarion becomes more ruthless and loses the more empathetic and vulnerable aspects of his character. From Victim to perpetrator in a heartbeat. That is why i compare him to a thinblood or Toredor, as soon as some of them gain real power they are some of the worst kindred imaginable.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T10:16:47-07:00","id":1541458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541411#post1541411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh look an old man yelling at clouds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541411#post1541411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Also, this is getting very US-specific)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately a good chunk of the Americans in the forums have no fucking clue of how the rest of the world works, barely remember we exist.<br /> <br /> But that's ok, I'm just being sad about people not using my correct pronouns, in the country where more people every year get killed for asking so. At least it isn't punishable by hanging by our law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T10:33:51-07:00","id":1541459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540831-vampire-bloodlines-2-videogame-delayed-again?p=1541401#post1541401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are missing my point when I say &quot;VtM is a Gen X thing&quot;. I agree completely that many of the themes are still relevant today if not more so.<br /> <br /> But what I am talking about is the people who inhabit those times and what they are rebelling against.<br /> <br /> VtM came out in the same era when the Cranberries released Zombie (a cultural touchstone for the Irish), REM released Losing My Religion which back then was rather taboo concept, the early 90s were still having aftershocks of the satanic panic and the religious groups burning D&amp;D books. We had the Bosnian genocide going on and Tiananmen square was still fresh in everyone's minds.<br /> <br /> The current crop of generations commemorate their struggles on social media with breaking down in tears at the concept of an 8-hour shift at starbucks, raging over the fact that other people don't believe in their pronouns, or being so socially stunted that the idea of talking to someone in person gives them anxiety on a generational level.<br /> <br /> As you can see this is night and day differences in cultural priorities between the different eras and generations. Now I don't consider this a bad thing, I look back at the 1960s &amp; the hippies and just don't get it, much to the annoyance of those who were there at the time.<br /> <br /> I agree the writers are a big part of the problem, but I feel it is a question of focus rather than inherent skill. VtM was created in a very specific cultural flavor which has now passed into history. The writers have a few choices to make with each new edition, do they cater to the original flavor and just work on improving the mechanics, or do they try to mutate the source material to fit whatever the current era is?<br /> <br /> The answer is to refine the mechanics, but not treat any era as the default. Just release splat books for eras that explains how each clan adjusts and how play styles change with advancing technology.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Moderator Warning: Leave this thread. We won't have any ridiculous classifications of entire generations here, thank you.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T10:35:41-07:00","id":1541460,"title":"","content":"Actually, sod it, I'm locking this thread. Its initial purpose as a news bulletin has been served, and has just gone on to fuel a two-page quagmire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}